-- title:
--   Crossing equation uv=varpi at singular points of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ given by [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot \mathrm{jNumQ}(q)$ of the modular invariant. Consider the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two maps $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the subalgebras $A[j]$-chart and $j^{-1}$-chart into the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $z$ be a point of this scheme and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ along `toBase`. Assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal{O}_z$ at $z$, and that $\mathcal{O}_z/(\varpi_z)$ is not a regular local ring. Then there exist $u, v \in \mathcal{O}_z$ with $uv = \varpi_z$ and with the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}_z$ equal to the ideal generated by $u$ and $v$.
--
--   This is the stalk-level form of the classical local description $\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_z \cong A[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi)$ of the integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ at a singular point of its fibre over $A$, the exponent being $1$ because $\zeta \in A$; it records that such a point is an ordinary double point whose two branches are cut out by $u$ and $v$. It feeds the statements that the germ of $\varpi$ lies in the square of the maximal ideal, the corresponding factorisation in localisations of the chart algebras, and the assembly of the properness, flatness, regularity and degeneration properties of the two-chart model.
